== 1 + 12^m is the midpoint (j = m) of the chain of 1 + 4^(2m) ==
   m = 1: T^(2m)(1 + 4^(2m)) = 13 = 1 + 12^m = 13: True; factors {13: 1}
   m = 2: T^(2m)(1 + 4^(2m)) = 145 = 1 + 12^m = 145: True; factors {5: 1, 29: 1}
   m = 3: T^(2m)(1 + 4^(2m)) = 1729 = 1 + 12^m = 1729: True; factors {7: 1, 13: 1, 19: 1}
   m = 4: T^(2m)(1 + 4^(2m)) = 20737 = 1 + 12^m = 20737: True; factors {89: 1, 233: 1}
   m = 5: T^(2m)(1 + 4^(2m)) = 248833 = 1 + 12^m = 248833: True; factors {13: 1, 19141: 1}
   m = 6: T^(2m)(1 + 4^(2m)) = 2985985 = 1 + 12^m = 2985985: True; factors {5: 1, 29: 1, 20593: 1}
